 "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AooCxcPxHQE",
 "title": "Sales 5 Step Follow Up Method",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "This video presents a five-step follow-up method for dealing with prospects who ghost you in sales. The creator outlines a system ranging from decision-making check-ins to breakup texts to move leads through the pipeline efficiently.",
 "key_points": [
  "Step 1: Ask if they have made a decision yet by referencing their stated problem and proposed solution.",
  "Step 2: Two days later, message them to figure out if the hesitation is due to timing, trust, or price, and handle objections accordingly.",
  "Step 3: A week later, send a personalized meme or GIF (using tools like Higgsfield and Kling 3.0) to grab attention.",
  "Step 4: Ask for permission to close your file if they still do not reply.",
  "Step 5: Send a breakup text explaining that the timing seems off, letting them know they can restart the conversation anytime if they want back in."
 ],
 "content": "The creator introduces a 5 touch follow up system for dealing with prospects who ghost you in sales. Step one is checking in on the decision: if no decision has been made, set up a decision-making call. You ask the prospect, \"You said that you were facing this problem and you have tried whatever that they have tried. This is our solution. Are we doing this?\" If they do not pick up the call, step two comes two days later where you message them to find out if it is a timing, trust, or price issue and handle the objection. Step three, if they have not responded a week later, is to send a meme or GIF. The creator recommends using Higgsfield and Kling 3.0 to generate a personalized video of yourself inside a meme or GIF, showing examples like a Superman-themed video captioned \"I tried calling you please call me back\" and a blinds video captioned \"Prospect said call me tomorrow, me tomorrow.\" Step four is asking for permission to close your file. Step five is sending a breakup text if they still do not reply because the goal is to get people out of the pipeline as quickly as possible. You tell them, \"hey man looks like the timing off right now if you ever want to get back in, just drop a text and then we can can restart having this conversation,\" which often prompts them to reply with a yes or that they need more time.",
 "status": "done",
